  "final_message": "The root cause was in `due_for_retry` in `billing/dunning.py`. Its filter was `status == \"open\" or (next_attempt_at is not None and next_attempt_at <= now)`. Because of the `or`, every open invoice was retried on every `run_cycle`, whatever its dunning schedule said.\n\nI changed that `or` to `and`. An invoice is now retried only when it is open and its `next_attempt_at` has arrived. That should stop the extra charges and let the subscription reach its final dunning state on schedule.\n\nThe 24 existing tests pass and ruff is clean. I didn't add a test for the retry schedule or run a failing-card scenario, so the \"4 attempts in the first week\" outcome is untested.\n\nI wrote `answer.json` as `{\"file\": \"dunning.py\", \"function\": \"due_for_retry\"}`.",
